4. Keystroke, mouse and session dimensions -- ORIGINAL WORK

   Collection uses native browser events (keydown/keyup, mousemove,
   mousedown/mouseup). No third-party behavioural biometrics library is
   used: dwell time is one subtraction from the browser's own timestamps,
   and writing it directly avoids any licensing question.

   Method reference (no code taken):
     Killourhy, K.S. & Maxion, R.A. (2009). "Comparing Anomaly-Detection
     Algorithms for Keystroke Dynamics." IEEE/IFIP DSN, 125-134.

   That benchmark found scaled Manhattan distance outperformed thirteen
   more sophisticated alternatives, which is why it is used here.
